# Waypoint Constraints

## Content

- `content/source/Master ATS Resume.md` is the factual source of truth.
- `content/work.ts`, `content/projects.ts`, and `content/profile.ts` must remain consistent with the source.
- Never fabricate facts, metrics, users, customers, architecture, technologies, responsibilities, outcomes, dates, or lessons.
- If source material does not support a claim, omit it rather than inventing it.

## Implementation

- Implement one bounded task at a time.
- Do not expand scope beyond the current task.
- Do not modify unrelated components.
- Prefer existing architecture and dependencies before introducing new ones.

## Validation

- Primary validation sequence: `npm run typecheck` → `npm run lint` → `npm run build`.
- There is currently no test framework.
- Do not install a test framework unless explicitly requested.

## Three.js

- Three.js is for storytelling and architecture visualization, not decoration.
- Keep geometry lightweight.
- No physics engines.
- No large textures or models unless explicitly required.
- Avoid expensive post-processing.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Provide graceful static fallback behavior.
- Critical content must remain semantic HTML outside WebGL.

## Design

- Warm off-white background (`#FAFAF8`).
- Near-black typography (`#171717`).
- Muted gray supporting elements.
- Restrained blue accent (`#2563eb`).
- Editorial, architectural, technical visual language.
- Structural borders preferred over card shadows.
- Avoid generic SaaS dashboard aesthetics.
- Avoid glassmorphism and excessive gradients.

## Accessibility

- Semantic HTML.
- Keyboard-accessible interactions.
- Visible focus states.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Do not communicate essential information through color alone.

## Performance

- Protect Core Web Vitals (LCP < 2.5s, CLS < 0.1, INP < 200ms).
- Avoid unnecessary client-side JavaScript.
- Lazy-load heavy visualizations.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies.
